---
/**
 * The project's own corrections log.
 *
 * The site records how everyone else's pages changed. This is the page where
 * it records how its own did. It is deliberately separate from
 * /record/changes/: that page is about the sources, and folding our errors
 * into it would bury them among four hundred entries about other people.
 *
 * Display data is precomputed here rather than branched in the template. Every
 * conditional in this file drives a `hidden` attribute; markup-returning
 * conditionals break Astro's expression parser and report the failure inside
 * the <style> block, which sends you hunting in the wrong file.
 */
import Article from '../layouts/Article.astro';
import { corrections, kindLabel, CORRECTIONS_SINCE } from '../lib/corrections';
import { isoToHuman } from '../lib/archive';

const CONTACT = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CONTACT || 'info@cc-vuln.org';

const KIND_CLASS: Record<string, string> = {
  correction: 'status--bad',
  clarification: 'status--info',
  withdrawal: 'status--neutral',
};

const entries = corrections().map((c) => ({
  ...c,
  when: isoToHuman(c.date),
  label: kindLabel(c.kind),
  badgeClass: `status ${KIND_CLASS[c.kind] ?? 'status--neutral'}`,
  hasSaid: Boolean(c.said),
  hasSays: Boolean(c.says),
  hasWhy: Boolean(c.why),
  hasCredit: Boolean(c.credit),
}));

const empty = entries.length === 0;
const openedOn = isoToHuman(CORRECTIONS_SINCE);
const count = entries.length === 1 ? '1 correction' : `${entries.length} corrections`;
---

<Article
  title="Corrections"
  description="Every correction to a published claim on this site, with what it said, what it says now, and what established the change."
  standfirst="What this project got wrong, what it says now, and what changed its mind."
  depth="plain"
  kicker="Corrections"
  next={{
    href: '/about/',
    label: 'About',
    note: 'Who publishes this, how evidence labels work, and where the evidence runs out.',
  }}
>
  <p>
    A record that grades its own claims has to be able to say where it got one
    wrong. Every correction to a material claim on this site is listed here,
    newest first, and marked on the page where the claim was. The two together
    are the policy: a log nobody passing the claim would see, or a quiet edit
    with no index, would each be half of it.
  </p>

  <p>
    This is not where sources changing their own pages go. That is the record's
    subject rather than an error of ours, and it is kept in the
    <a href="/record/changes/">source change record</a>, with the underlying
    captures preserved either way. Rewording, restructuring and tooling changes
    are in <a href="https://github.com/cc-vuln/coldcard-rng-incident" rel="noopener">the repository history</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    Corrections are welcome and are the most useful thing anyone can send.
    Name the page and the claim, say what is wrong, and include something
    another reader can check: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
    Whoever reports a correction is credited here if they want to be. A claim
    is never quietly deleted: what it said stays on this page.
  </p>

  <div class="ve-card ve-card--recessed" hidden={!empty}>
    <div class="ve-card__label lbl-blue">Nothing logged yet</div>
    <p>
      This log opened on {openedOn} and holds no entries. That records the
      state of the log, not a claim that the site has never been wrong: changes
      made before it opened are in the repository history, where every edit to
      every page is dated and attributable to a commit.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="mono-label" hidden={empty}>{count} since {openedOn}</p>

  <ol class="corr" hidden={empty}>
    {entries.map((c) => (
      <li class="corr__item">
        <div class="corr__head">
          <span class={c.badgeClass}>{c.label}</span>
          <time datetime={c.date}>{c.when}</time>
        </div>
        <p class="corr__summary">{c.summary}</p>
        <dl class="corr__detail">
          <div class="corr__row" hidden={!c.hasSaid}>
            <dt>It said</dt>
            <dd>{c.said}</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="corr__row" hidden={!c.hasSays}>
            <dt>It says now</dt>
            <dd>{c.says}</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="corr__row" hidden={!c.hasWhy}>
            <dt>Why</dt>
            <dd>{c.why}</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="corr__row" hidden={!c.hasCredit}>
            <dt>Reported by</dt>
            <dd>{c.credit}</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="corr__row">
            <dt>Where</dt>
            <dd>
              {c.pages.map((page) => (
                <a class="corr__page" href={page}>{page}</a>
              ))}
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <h2 id="how-corrections-are-handled">How a correction is handled</h2>

  <ol>
    <li>
      The claim is rechecked against the artefact it cites, not against the
      argument for it. If the artefact does not support the claim, the claim is
      wrong however reasonable it sounded.
    </li>
    <li>
      The page is changed where the claim was, keeping its
      <a href="/about/#claim-statuses">evidence marker</a> honest: a claim that
      turns out to rest on someone's say-so becomes reported, not verified.
    </li>
    <li>
      An entry is added here with the published wording that was wrong, so the
      correction can be checked rather than taken on trust.
    </li>
    <li>
      Captures are never rewritten. The archive is append-only, so a correction
      changes what this site says about a source and never what the source was
      recorded as saying.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    Requests to remove correctly reported material are not corrections and are
    not honoured: what a party published is the record. The limits of that are
    set out on <a href="/about/#displayed-captures">the About page</a>.
  </p>
</Article>

<style>
  .corr { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  .corr__item {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface); padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
  }
  .corr__item + .corr__item { margin-top: .9rem; }
  .corr__head {
    display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: .7rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .72rem; color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .corr__summary { margin-top: .6rem; font-weight: 500; }
  .corr__detail {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
    gap: .35rem .9rem; margin-top: .8rem;
    font-size: .85rem; line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .corr__row { display: contents; }
  .corr__row[hidden] { display: none; }
  .corr__detail dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .64rem;
    letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-3); padding-top: .25rem;
  }
  .corr__detail dd { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .corr__page { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .78rem; }
  .corr__page + .corr__page { margin-left: .6rem; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .corr__detail { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: .1rem; }
    .corr__detail dd { margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  }
</style>
